 "title": "Уход с праздника  (Leaving the Party)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "nastya": "Настя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The restaurant's party is in full swing, but Nastya has had enough and is heading for the door. Kostya catches up with her, because he has something to say. We'll hear it in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Настя, подожди!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Не уходи так быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "У меня много дел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я хочу поговорить с тобой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "О чем ты хочешь поговорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Это очень важно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Говори быстрее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Подойди поближе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я слушаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я не могу молчать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, выслушай меня.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's replay it step by step.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Настя, подожди!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nastya, wait!' The command is the casual one. Kostya calls out her name first.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bye.' The word 'poka' is the casual goodbye, which Nastya says without looking back.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, are you leaving already?' The word for 'leave' is the ongoing kind, for going away, and 'already' is a small word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yeah. It's a bit of a downer here.' The word 'aga' is a casual 'yeah'. The word for 'dull' is made by putting 'ne' in front of 'cheerful'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Не уходи так быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't leave so fast.' The word for a negative command uses the ongoing kind, and 'so fast' is two small words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "У меня много дел.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I've got a lot to do.' The word for 'matters' loses its ending after 'many', and 'at me' stands for 'I have'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я хочу поговорить с тобой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I want to talk to you.' The word for 'with you' is the irregular 'toboy', and the word for 'I want' is irregular too.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "О чем ты хочешь поговорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you want to talk about?' The words for 'about what' sound like one. The word for 'you want' ends in 'sh'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Это очень важно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's very important.' 'Important' ends in 'o', without a subject. 'Very' is placed in front.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Говори быстрее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Speak faster.' The word for 'faster' is made from 'quickly' with 'ee', and the word for 'speak' is the casual command.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Подойди поближе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come a bit closer.' The 'po' prefix makes 'closer' into 'a bit closer'. 'Come up' has a prefix too.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я слушаю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm listening.' The word for 'I listen' is a single word, and it ends in 'yu'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я не могу молчать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I can't keep quiet.' The word for 'I can't' is irregular, and 'keep quiet' is the plain form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Пожалуйста, выслушай меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Please hear me out.' 'Hear out' has the prefix 'vy', meaning 'to the end'. 'Please' is the longer word. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Настя, подожди!",
   "gap": 0.5
